From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WavJaby <WavJaby@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 20:00:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(angle): give each context its own native context

- DisplayEGL::createContext: a context without
  EGL_CONTEXT_VIRTUALIZATION_GROUP_ANGLE gets a renderer of its own
  (createRenderer), native-shared with its share context, or with
  mRenderer under EGL_DISPLAY_TEXTURE_SHARE_GROUP_ANGLE, as the group
  path does. A virtualization group still shares one renderer
- Cost: one native context per ANGLE context

Upstream-Status: Pending
Patch-Reason: a native context is current on one thread at a time:
 eglMakeCurrent with a context bound to another thread fails with
 EGL_BAD_ACCESS (Mesa eglcontext.c). ANGLE's default shares mRenderer's
 one native context among all contexts, and display init leaves it
 current on the initialising thread (makeNewContextCurrent). Measured
 in the ATL app gate: the first eglMakeCurrent of an app context fails
 with EGL_BAD_ACCESS under ANGLE, and the same call succeeds without
 ANGLE (selection on vs off). Cause inferred, not yet logged: another
 thread holds the shared native context (hwui's RenderThread is the
 likely holder). A loader or environment switch cannot pick the
 renderer: the app's attribute does it, and ANGLE has no feature flag
 for a default. The driver-side alternative (per-thread host contexts
 in libGLES_atl) is a new mechanism in our layer.
---
SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
 src/libANGLE/renderer/gl/egl/DisplayEGL.cpp | 17 +++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/libANGLE/renderer/gl/egl/DisplayEGL.cpp b/src/libANGLE/renderer/gl/egl/DisplayEGL.cpp
index 732b7c92cea6f1a0896eea40ec093e09264877b9..ef3cb4ad13accc5591d0879e9dbe8399f02d70e8 100644
--- a/src/libANGLE/renderer/gl/egl/DisplayEGL.cpp
+++ b/src/libANGLE/renderer/gl/egl/DisplayEGL.cpp
@@ -498,7 +498,10 @@ ContextImpl *DisplayEGL::createContext(const gl::State &state,
     bool globalTextureShareGroup =
         attribs.get(EGL_DISPLAY_TEXTURE_SHARE_GROUP_ANGLE, EGL_FALSE) == EGL_TRUE;
 
-    std::shared_ptr<RendererEGL> renderer = mRenderer;
+    // Android: a context without a virtualization group gets a renderer (native context) of its
+    // own, not mRenderer's. EGL binds a native context to one thread at a time, so a shared one
+    // held by another thread fails every other thread's eglMakeCurrent. A group still shares one.
+    std::shared_ptr<RendererEGL> renderer;
     if (usingExternalContext)
     {
         ASSERT(!shareContext);
@@ -509,9 +512,12 @@ ContextImpl *DisplayEGL::createContext(const gl::State &state,
             return nullptr;
         }
     }
-    else if (virtualizationGroup != EGL_DONT_CARE)
+    else
     {
-        renderer = mVirtualizationGroups[virtualizationGroup].lock();
+        if (virtualizationGroup != EGL_DONT_CARE)
+        {
+            renderer = mVirtualizationGroups[virtualizationGroup].lock();
+        }
         if (!renderer)
         {
             // If the user requested a dispaly-level texture share group, all contexts must be in
@@ -535,7 +541,10 @@ ContextImpl *DisplayEGL::createContext(const gl::State &state,
                 return nullptr;
             }
 
-            mVirtualizationGroups[virtualizationGroup] = renderer;
+            if (virtualizationGroup != EGL_DONT_CARE)
+            {
+                mVirtualizationGroups[virtualizationGroup] = renderer;
+            }
         }
     }
     ASSERT(renderer);
